<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Gotha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1601">1601</a>–<a href="/years/1675">1675</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ernest the Pious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest I, called the Pious, founded the Duchy of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> in 1640. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War he rebuilt his lands as a model Lutheran state, introducing compulsory schooling and orderly administration from Friedenstein Castle in Gotha. In 1680 his seven sons divided his inheritance, creating the duchies of Gotha, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romhild">Römhild</a>, Eisenberg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildburghausen">Hildburghausen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha.jpg" alt="Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Gotha" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernest_I,_duke_of_Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
